    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d379-a3">

                <pb facs="0614" n="544" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg544"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 28, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Romero said that he read with attention the memorandum of the Examiner of
                    Claims of the department, handed to him by Mr. Seward; that Mr. Romero thinks it
                    very reasonable, so far as it admits that a government has the right to impress
                    the money of the residents, when in extreme need of it, just as it can impress
                    horses, ships, &amp;c, this right being one of eminent domain; that Mr. Romero
                    has no instructions from his government to begin or enter into negotiations with
                    the government of the United States for the purpose contemplated in said
                    memorandum; but that he will submit that paper to the Mexican government, and
                    will ask for instructions on the subject, and that, in the meanwhile, the
                    negotiation may be considered as commenced.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
